Changelog: 21-10-2026 14:25:29

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 21-10-2026 13:23:31

Added. SameBoy Manager: Game Boy and Game Boy Color games on the BC-250 with the SameBoy core of RetroArch (SameBoy
releases no Linux build). As SwanStation Manager does, the app installs RetroArch from Flathub (a Flatpak, for the user,
or uses the one that is installed) and the core from the libretro build server (checked as a zip with one x86-64 Linux
library; the build server keeps only the newest build, so the core is not pinned: the app records its build date and
SHA-256, says when there is a newer build, also in the portal's notice of updates outside the suite, and installs it on
Update). No BIOS is needed. It finds the games in the chosen folders (.gb and .gbc files, and .zip files with one in
them, told by the cartridge header's checksum and ROM size, the system from its colour flag) and puts the ticked ones in
Steam for Game Mode, "[GB] Title" or "[GBC] Title", the artwork drawn from the app's icon. The Game Mode shortcuts run
~/.local/bin/bc250-sameboy-run, which starts the RetroArch Flatpak with the core (--fullscreen) and, when Steam starts a
game on a Wayland desktop, without RetroArch's Wayland socket so Steam's overlay works. Not tried on the board yet: a
game from Game Mode, a zipped game, the controllers under Steam Input.
